{"toolCallId":"call_1505f5525ce443e8a3e4b3f4b49a809b","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"[speckit] Skipping branch creation (--skip-branch)\ndescription.json created in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  SpecKit: Spec Folder Created Successfully\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  BRANCH_NAME:  001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n  FEATURE_NUM:  001\n  DOC_LEVEL:    Level 3\n  SPEC_FOLDER:  /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n\n  Created Structure:\n  └── 001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/\n      ├── spec.md\n      ├── plan.md\n      ├── tasks.md\n      ├── implementation-summary.md\n      ├── acceptance-criteria.md\n      ├── description.json\n      ├── description.json   (per-folder identity)\n      └── scratch/          (working files; NOT git-ignored)\n          └── .gitkeep\n\n  Level 3 Documentation (manifest-backed Level contract):\n    ✓ Core: spec.md + plan.md + tasks.md\n    ✓ Lifecycle: implementation-summary.md (scaffolded; required after implementation starts)\n    ✓ +Verify: merged verification/testing in tasks.md, NFRs, edge cases\n    ✓ +Arch: executive summary, risk matrix, decision guidance\n      (Architecture decisions - adds ~150 LOC)\n\n  Next steps:\n    1. Fill out spec.md with requirements\n    2. Create implementation plan in plan.md\n    3. Break down tasks in tasks.md\n    4. Add verification items to tasks.md\n    5. Add on-demand docs with --with-lazy-addons when needed\n    6. Add goal.md with --with-goal or /create:goal when an operator will set this packet as a session objective\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"32bcf2","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_194e875390f344a0ba346d6c8185d789","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"41:const BACKFILL = '.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/graph/backfill-graph-metadata.ts';\n42:const TSX_LOADER = './.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs';\n67://   GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE is structural and included, because the re-derive\n85:// The subset a re-derive can actually settle, because they are assertions about\n87:// in-document reference paths, which a re-derive does not write; planning one\n121:// exit code counts it. Carries no apply(): the re-derive is a child process the\n123:const REDERIVE_STEP = Object.freeze({ what: 're-derive graph metadata' });\n248:// Measured set: the packet files the re-derive child opened through planted links. Mirrors the packet document lists of the graph parser, the drift check and folder discovery.\n435:  // not one, and a re-derive computes null. The graph merge keeps a stored\n436:  // parent over a null re-derive and flags it for review, so after a move the\n445:      // A graph file that cannot be read is the re-derive's to report.\n483:async function rederive(folder) {\n485:    await run('node', ['--import', TSX_LOADER, BACKFILL, folder], CHILD);\n514:  // re-derive is part of the repair rather than a follow-up; skipping it swaps\n519:  // re-derive into a packet whose graph file is a link would replace the link with a\n520:  // regular file. A linked graph file is therefore never re-derived, and the dry run\n523:  const rederiveNeeded = !graphIsLink && (edits.length > 0 || staleMetadata);\n524:  const planned = rederiveNeeded ? [...edits, REDERIVE_STEP] : [...edits];\n550:    // A link among the re-derive's inputs is refused here, whether it was present at planning or\n554:    const reason = linked.length > 0 ? `${linked[0]}: ${SYMLINK_REFUSAL}` : await rederive(folder);\n555:    if (reason && !failure) failure = `re-derive: ${reason}`;\n673:  const required = apply ? [VALIDATE, BACKFILL] : [VALIDATE];\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w904a7ae601/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"1aa9ce","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
